==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*8 [[Dagshund]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 12~18 seconds<sup>360f~540f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 7.33~12.67 seconds<sup>220f~380f</sup>.
*1 [[Henry]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Henry]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Henry]] spawns after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A recommended lineup is [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cat]] along with fast damage dealers such as [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or even [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] if at a high enough level. "Research" Effect UP [[Cat Combo|Combos]] such as [[Cheating Heart? (Combo)|Cheating Heart?]] are recommended for your spammable cats.

[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] is also a great unit for this stage, with Massive Damage against Traitless and Freeze immunity, meaning you don't have to time him against the Henries.

If you somehow have [[Brainwashed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Flying Cat]], he'll make this stage pretty easy with his slow since almost every enemy here has less range than him.

On the off chance you have [[Dark Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Gothic Mitama]] - send her out after upgrading the [[Worker Cat]] to level 2 and send a Cyborg + Seafarer Cat to deal with the first few peons. Then start spawning [[Delinquent Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ultra Delinquent Cats]] as much as possible. It should take you a few minutes to clear this stage, but there is no shortage of money.

